  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Crop Breeding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve crop breeding in low- and middle-income countries by using advanced computer-based tools to speed up the identification and selection of useful plant traits. Working in partnership with UK researchers, international agricultural research centres and local research organisations, the project will test new approaches for analysing plant genetics to support the development of crops that are more resilient to climate change and better suited to local farming needs.  It will compare the benefits of these AI-enabled methods with existing breeding practices. The work will also help build skills and knowledge among national research partners so they can use these technologies independently in future. By strengthening local scientific capacity and improving breeding methods, the project will contribute to more reliable food production, stronger rural livelihoods and long-term climate and development goals.</narrative>
  </description>
